2026-09-23 — T03c independent metadata/proof replay audit.

Scope: EvoIR 1.9.105 Sections 2/3/4/5/7/8/9/11 and EvoMIR 0.35's
corresponding placement, ABI and symbol contracts, as exercised by the existing
copy_is_opaque integration test. This is not an audit of every spec clause.

The previous mutations generally retained the original output digest; most
did not explicitly establish that a producer-controlled replacement digest
also fails. The checker already reconstructs from the original module rather
than trusting that digest. No production checker defect was found here.

Each candidate now parses, validates and renders canonically. Its changed
output digest must differ from the valid baseline, and the written certificate
is reparsed to prove its claimed digest matches the candidate bytes. Thus a
producer-only hash check ACCEPTS the control, while the real independent
checker must return semantic-rejection exit 3, not parse-error 2 or a crash.
The input module, rewrite proof, registry and budget remain unchanged.

37 independently rejected changes:
  function patch placement and section                  6
  HFA versus HVA/member format                          2
  floating NaN payload, operation and conversion guard   3
  HFA natural transport alignment                       2
  SIMD assembly constraint and clobber                   2
  AES round versus inverse                              1
  lifecycle priority/root/phase/function/tie order, TLS  9
  atomic order and replacement with ordinary store       2
  vector lane and public HVA ABI                         3
  visibility of global/extern/declare/alias/function      5
  volatile representation-read versus write             1
  same-typed indirect-edge storage address                1

All 13 Rust tests pass, including 14 positive replay controls (the alignment
test has two baselines). Lifecycle coverage includes equal-priority ordering;
TLS coverage includes changing an actual tls_addr target, not only its model.
The initial expanded fixture had an extra blank line in its global table;
that fixture-format error was corrected, not reported as a compiler defect.

Changed gate against 235c031: 44 PASS, 0 FAIL, 0 ignored in 8 groups;
Clippy --all-targets -D warnings and workspace fmt PASS. Temporary test files
are removed by the existing RAII helper. No VM, source copy or campaign ran.
T03's wider audit and R01 whole-kernel certificates remain open.
